      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-104007",
      ":question/problem": "The vector-valued function $f(\\theta ,\u03d5),$ given by \n\n$$\nf(\\theta ,\u03d5)=\u27e84\\operatorname{cosh}\u2061\u03d5\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta ,\\,\\text{_____},\\,4\\operatorname{sinh}\u2061\u03d5\u27e9\n$$\n\nparametrizes the hyperboloid of one sheet defined in Cartesian coordinates as ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}=16.$ By expressing the equation of the hyperboloid in cylindrical polar coordinates, determine the second component of $f.$\n\n*Hint: You may use the fact that the hyperbola ${r}^{2}-{z}^{2}={k}^{2}$ can be parametrized as $\u27e8r,z\u27e9=\u27e8k\\operatorname{cosh}\u2061\u03d5,k\\operatorname{sinh}\u2061\u03d5\u27e9$* for $\u03d5\\in R.$"
